# Managed by Ansible (clamav role) — do not edit by hand.
# Deliberately omits NotifyClamd (which the image's stock config sets): this
# deployment runs no clamd daemon, so every refresh warned "Clamd was NOT
# notified: Can't connect to clamd through /tmp/clamd.sock".
# UpdateLogFile is omitted too — output goes to stdout, which the wrapper
# script appends to {{ clamav_log_dir }}/freshclam.log.
#
# DatabaseOwner root (not the image default `clamav`, UID 100): Ansible owns
# the DB dir as {{ username }}, so a freshclam that drops to UID 100 cannot
# write its temp dir and fails with rc=10. The image's init wrapper used to
# paper over this by chown-ing the mount on every run; we bypass that wrapper,
# so state ownership stays stable instead. The container is throwaway and only
# has the DB dir mounted rw.
DatabaseOwner root
DatabaseMirror database.clamav.net
ScriptedUpdates yes
